{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362335-trinity-vs-they-came-from-beneath-the-sea","id":1362335,"title":"Trinity vs. They Came From Beneath the Sea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-20T21:24:48-08:00","id":1362335,"title":"Trinity vs. They Came From Beneath the Sea","content":"So: <b>They Came From Beneath the Sea</b> is almost out now: backer previews have been released. It has been cited as the game that made the Trinity devs take a step back from producing a 50s era. Still, I find myself wondering about how the two games might be brought together. <br /> <br /> Back in its 1e days, one of the devs for Adventure! was pushing the notion that Daredevils aren't some sort of \u201cempowered human\u201d; that Dramatic Editing and Heroic Knacks were metagaming constructs that represented genre conventions rather than in-setting phenomena. For better or worse, Trinity Continuum has gone the other way, with Talents being subconscious reality manipulators. But in contrast to this, <b>They Came From Beneath the Sea</b> has gone all in on the \u201cgenre conventions\u201d and meaning thing: its equivalent of Dramatic Editing is \u201cDirectorial Control\u201d. With this in mind, its protagonists are more like Talents than psychics or superhumans. Indeed, the extent to which psychic or superhuman phenomena show up, they're presented as something that's (sorry for the pun, but not really) Fishy. <br /> <br /> So with that in mind: how do the two compare and contrast as you see them; and what can be borrowed from each to enrich the other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T21:43:51-08:00","id":1362339,"title":"","content":"I'll mostly mine it for sea-based Aberrents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T02:23:24-08:00","id":1362371,"title":"","content":"My first impressions (and I don\u2019t have seconds as I didn\u2019t read it properly) are very positive.<br /> <br /> The dramatic edition rules are better established and are more restrictive, but they are more frequent (at least looks like). That is a thing I would like to bring to Talents and don\u2019t know how.<br /> <br /> The weapons, or the lack of them, is interesting. Knowing the system I know how to build some weapons, but not sure how other players may deal with it. Probably fine as the idea of the game is more important than the rules, but I am still very rules oriented. It\u2019s interesting how the game can work, I certainly would use this idea for some random things, but not sure how or what for yet.<br /> <br /> The sea monsters are awesome. The way they work and the way they managed to put all the sea monsters from movies in a single book... I really could use some of the ideas in Adventure, probably not in Core as they don\u2019t really fit into it (as I see).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T09:51:52-08:00","id":1362430,"title":"","content":"I'm loving They Came From Beneath the Sea also.<br /> <br /> One of the significant changes I see is the Damage Rating/Injury Level and Shrug it Off systems. Still considering how it plays. Seems to by a nice Hybrid of Storypath and Old World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T10:18:52-08:00","id":1362442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362335-trinity-vs-they-came-from-beneath-the-sea?p=1362430#post1362430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm loving They Came From Beneath the Sea also.<br /> <br /> One of the significant changes I see is the Damage Rating/Injury Level and Shrug it Off systems. Still considering how it plays. Seems to by a nice Hybrid of Storypath and Old World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone who hasn't had a chance to grab TCFBTS yet, what's the high level on Damage Rating/Injury Level and Shrug it Off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T11:04:00-08:00","id":1362465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1362335-trinity-vs-they-came-from-beneath-the-sea?p=1362442#post1362442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As someone who hasn't had a chance to grab TCFBTS yet, what's the high level on Damage Rating/Injury Level and Shrug it Off?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Weapons &amp; Damage Rating</b><br /> Most weapons are 1 Enhancement per decription text, up to 3 with enhancements. I do not see a weapons list or armor list, that is not the focus. There are weapon tags and armor tags. Damage rating are generated with the succcesses. A successful attack gives you a damage rating of 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Indirect Damage</b><br /> Burning house is 3-4 Damage Rating, falling is 1 per 3m, Cobra Venom 5, Reactor Leak 5 (highest)<br /> There are direct rating to Shrug Off or not, no attack roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Armor</b><br /> Armor gices you enhanements on Shrug it Off to resist Damage Ratings.<br /> <br /> <b>Stunt</b><br /> INCREASE DAMAGE (VARIABLE)<br /> You find a sensitive spot, which inflicts more damage.<br /> Each success increases the attack\u2019s damage rating by +1.<br /> <br /> <b>Shrug it Off</b><br /> Say a punch does 3 damage rating, then you can Shrug Off the Damage Rating with a resistance roll (usually stamina) to reduce it (1 for 1). However if an effect does an injury level it bypasses the Damage Rating/Shrug it Off and fills up the level.<br /> <br /> <b>Health Track</b><br /> Here is the Health Track which makes a destinction between Injury Levels Flesh Wound, That'll Leave a Scar, etc and the Damage Rating (3 boxes) within each Injury Level. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Just A Flesh Wound</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">OOO</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+1 Archtype Dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">That'11 Leave A Scar</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">OOO</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2 Archtype Dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Last Ditch Effort</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">OOO</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2/+3 Archtype Dice</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">O</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Remember Me</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">OOO</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+3 Any Pool</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Death Scene</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"></td> </tr> </table></div> Seems like a Hybrid of Storypath, OWOD/CO as essential additional success equal damage.<br /> <br /> The writing and presentation are amazing. Really story driven, I can't wait for the final hardback and than They Came From Beneath the Grave.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 01-21-2020, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T11:40:08-08:00","id":1362472,"title":"","content":"That is a great way to deal damage on a less \u201call or nothing\u201d effect. I had a quick look on it but didn\u2019t pay much attention. Now I will go back with much more attention...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T12:13:11-08:00","id":1362480,"title":"","content":"It's a good example of a 1950s Trinity Continuum setting. You could use the TCFBTS rules to create <i>kaiju </i>(giant monsters) like Godzilla and Mothra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T12:23:35-08:00","id":1362482,"title":"","content":"We need a They Came From Beneath The ..... forum and a Dystopia Rising forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T12:45:30-08:00","id":1362487,"title":"","content":"Yeah; well, we're not getting one. From what I hear, these forms are broken and limping along. One ability that they've lost is to make new forums. So don't expect They Came From\u2026 or Dystopia Rising; don't expect a Storypath umbrella forum with Trinity, Scion, etc. below it; heck, you can't even expect a Deviant: the Renegades subforum under the Chronicles of Darkness umbrella forum. Because, for reasons that escape me, that's no longer possible. The most you can expect is the renaming of existing forums, as was recently done with what was originally the Pugmire and Cavaliers of Mars forum and is now Partner Games.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/trouble-tickets/1335735-no-dystopia-rising-revolution-forum?p=1343244#post1343244\">Here's the supporting post.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-21-2020, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Post